WEBVTT

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:49.070
Whoa!

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:55.530
Sorry.

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:33.480
<i>"TTT..."?</i>

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:34.900
<i>Is it some kind of memo?</i>

00:01:55.760 --> 00:02:00.930
I walk unsteadily on paths to nowhere

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:05.060
wondering what I should do right now.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:11.520
I play the song you like on the car stereo

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:16.070
with the volume up and my feelings crystallized

00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:21.700
driving on streets with no crossroads or signals

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:27.120
with a speed that will catch up with you.

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:31.580
So faraway - let's run!

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:37.880
And let's not bother with the breaks - full throttle.

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:42.180
Oh someday - one of these days

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:47.270
You'll be at my place where nobody can find you.

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:53.360
Whenever you suffer a breakdown one can't see

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:58.950
depend on me for your repairs.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:03.320
So faraway - let's run!

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:09.540
We'll reset and start again - even at our limit.

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:13.840
Oh someday - one of these days

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:19.880
If I'm with you we'll find our dream.

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:30.230
A Girl Named Sara

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:47.080
You're late, Patric.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:52.330
<i>Is that guy a detective?</i>

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:55.840
Thanks for waiting.

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:58.090
Hmm?

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:00.090
That is not right, Monsieur.

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:06.100
Not every <i>parisienne</i> sitting in a café
intends to attract a <i>parisien</i> out on the town.

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:08.100
That girl is only fifteen.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.100
And besides, she is Patric's woman.

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:12.520
Patric?

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:14.350
He steals wallets at the Métro.

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:19.820
That fellow always partners himself with a
nice-looking novice that won't attract attention

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:22.820
and passes them the stolen money while on the train.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:24.610
That scoundrel is quite shrewd.

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:29.870
Besides, you can't keep staring at a girl like that.

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:34.540
If you want get yourself a <i>parisienne</i> you need to smile.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:35.880
Smile.

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:42.470
Huh?

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:35.600
Don't make a fuss.

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:37.690
I'm sure you witnessed it.

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:40.440
I was the one who killed that man on the Métro.

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:43.690
You don't want his fate, do you?

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:50.240
You still have the wallet that Patric stole, don't you?

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:51.160
Hand it over!

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:52.700
What are you saying?

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:54.370
You wanna die?

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:55.450
Stop.

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:01.750
You were...

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:06.970
Carnac sent me.

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:09.590
You gonna give me the goods, Bazaine?

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:11.640
It's right here.

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:13.970
It's also been dissolved in sterilized water.

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:16.730
Please tell Carnac that.

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:17.980
All right.

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:21.230
And my 30,000 euros?

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:26.990
First you must hand over that memo with the info needed to replicate the DNA.

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:27.780
Of course.

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:28.740
I have it right here...

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:30.990
What's wrong?

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:33.580
It's... It's stolen.

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:36.290
He stole my wallet I kept that memo in.

00:06:36.290 --> 00:06:37.200
What?

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:39.790
It... It was that boy.

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:42.000
What'll we do? What'll we do?

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:45.170
Don't worry, I'll get it back for you.

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:49.300
So you just sit back, relax... and die!

00:06:57.180 --> 00:07:00.940
Oh, hey! What's wrong? You all right?

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:03.440
Huh, he's sound asleep!

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:10.950
Heh.

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:13.700
Still, you picked the right time to come.

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:16.200
Now I don't have to spend time looking for you.

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:19.710
Don't move!

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:45.860
Next on the news, at around 4:15 this afternoon

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:45.860
<i>Why does that man know about me and Patric?</i>

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:49.360
A 30-year-old Paris university
researcher, a Mr. Henri Bazaine

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:52.360
was found dead in the Métro inside a Line 1 train.

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:58.370
He most likely died due to loss of blood caused by a bullet shot at close range.

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:01.370
Henri Bazaine... that was him!

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:08.420
...lately on the same line there has been a string of pickpocketings committed by an organized group.

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:11.630
Patric stole that man's wallet.

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:17.010
<i>And that other man wanted that wallet.</i>

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:19.140
<i>He wanted that memo.</i>

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:23.890
We might have gotten ourselves involved in something very serious!

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:27.400
Why aren't you calling, Patric?

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:38.910
Dammit, that bastard.

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:40.790
Next time I see you, you're dead.

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:46.040
All right, see you later!

00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:00.140
Ah, it's you.

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:06.600
Please.

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:17.990
Wh...

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:19.030
Who are you?!

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:23.290
You...

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:27.040
I see. Quite a hideout you got here.

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:31.300
What do you want?

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:36.300
Sara still has the wallet you stole in the subway, doesn't she Patric?

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:40.850
Call Sara and tell her to bring the wallet.

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:42.010
And be quick about it!

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:44.560
I don't know Sara's number-

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:48.810
You want me to break your arms next?

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:50.110
All right, I'll do it!

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:56.650
Hello, Sara?

00:09:56.650 --> 00:09:58.610
Yeah, it's me.

00:09:58.610 --> 00:09:59.700
Run!

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:00.830
Get out of there right now!

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:06.540
Now what, huh?

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:10.420
Now even I don't know where Sara is!

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:13.380
Beat me up all you want, it'll be no use!

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:14.880
So you can take it, huh?

00:10:15.630 --> 00:10:20.890
And nobody can hear you from the outside no matter how much you scream, right?

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:24.890
Pa... Patric?

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:39.490
I'll ask you once more.

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:46.410
She usually waits for you at the Champs-Élysées or the Arc de Triomphe Métro entrances, doesn't she?

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:47.540
Yeah...

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:50.750
And you two always meet at exactly 5:00 at night?

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:52.000
Uh... yeah...

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:55.630
If I find you've been lying to me...

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:58.170
I... I'm not lying!

00:10:58.170 --> 00:10:58.880
It's all true!

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:03.890
All right, I believe you.

00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:06.140
You can rest easy now.

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:29.910
That man!

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:45.140
Get in.

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:46.720
Wh... Who are-

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:47.640
Don't delay.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:58.070
Dammit!

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:15.040
If you don't want to die, stay in here.

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:16.960
Why?

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:19.300
Why are you helping me?

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:20.050
Who are you?

00:12:23.090 --> 00:12:25.640
Why is he trying to kill me?

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:26.930
I didn't do anything!

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:53.080
Sorry, Mr. Carnac.

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:54.580
I have the goods, but...

00:12:58.090 --> 00:13:00.340
Y... You!

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:02.340
Tell Carnac:

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:07.340
"The girl with the memo is at the Hotel Bouffant on Montmartre Avenue."

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:08.850
Wh-What did you say?

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:10.350
What the hell are you-

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:19.520
Looks like Carnac has gotten the message. Now leave.

00:13:37.880 --> 00:13:39.000
You... bastard!

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:01.270
Where are we going?

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:02.780
Where are you planning to take me?

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:06.030
You have no choice but to trust me.

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:08.030
If you value your life.

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:10.280
No I don't!

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:14.290
Adults... men... all of you are liars!

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:20.290
Even Patric, the one guy I thought had my back, ended up abandoning me.

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:22.290
Patric was killed.

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:22.920
Huh?

00:14:26.920 --> 00:14:28.930
P... Patric?

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:33.930
"The police are looking for a missing girl." Do they mean me?

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:40.940
This article says Patric and I killed that man in the subway, stole his wallet...

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:44.440
...and that I double-crossed Patric and killed him.

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:49.860
And if you die, that's how they'll conclude the case.

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:50.450
No way!

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:58.120
I should have just tossed this memo.

00:14:58.120 --> 00:15:00.670
They'll come after you no matter what you do.

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:04.630
They intend to eliminate every person who saw that.

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:07.710
There's no other path for you to take.

00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:12.220
I'm not telling you to believe me like the adults and men you despise.

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:16.640
But this time, you have no choice but to trust me.

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:27.190
Um, my name is Sara Perriand.

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:30.240
Yes, I've been told.

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:35.870
Welcome back.

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:51.930
Who's there?

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:53.090
It's Édith.

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:05.060
Did you find out Carnac's whereabouts?

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:10.610
This is Carnac's handwriting.

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:16.870
I'm sure you know what Carnac plans to do based on that.

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:18.410
What can I say?

00:16:18.410 --> 00:16:21.250
Everything's a virtual game to him.

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:24.250
He's went off on his own,

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:29.250
and stole the funds from our group in order to carry out his destructive activities.

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:31.010
He's both treacherous and dangerous.

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:35.260
You're the only one who can stop him.

00:16:36.260 --> 00:16:39.260
I see the time has finally come.

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:42.270
He is certain to come here looking for this girl.

00:16:43.310 --> 00:16:46.020
Even if he knows that it will be an ambush.

00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:50.030
Is there anything I can do to help?

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:54.280
As long as you confirmed that memo, we're good.

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:58.280
Leave before he sees you.

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:01.290
You don't need to worry.

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:03.910
Even she knows.

00:17:03.910 --> 00:17:07.540
She can't save herself unless she goes through with this.

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:28.810
Get in the bathroom.

00:17:29.440 --> 00:17:30.070
Huh?

00:17:30.070 --> 00:17:31.070
Hurry.

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:39.580
I'm fine, I ain't drunk I tell you!

00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:42.200
Please sir, can you keep it down?

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:44.330
Keep it down, you say?!

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:47.830
We can't disturb the other guests this late at night.

00:17:56.970 --> 00:17:59.970
Hey, this is me you're talking to, pal!

00:18:01.220 --> 00:18:03.220
I'm sorry for disturbing you.

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:04.220
Hey.

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:04.980
Carnac, right?

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:07.230
Carnac?

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:09.980
I don't go by that stupid name.

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:12.230
I'm <i>the</i> Thoreau Albert!

00:18:12.230 --> 00:18:13.360
Okay, okay.

00:18:13.360 --> 00:18:15.860
You better remember that!

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:21.370
How did you know I was Carnac?

00:18:21.990 --> 00:18:27.620
I don't wait in a hotel without checking the employee roster first.

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:29.630
I see.

00:18:29.630 --> 00:18:32.630
So that's why you picked such a tiny hotel.

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:39.130
That's what I'd do if I called someone over without knowing what he looked like.

00:18:39.890 --> 00:18:42.100
I'm impressed.

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:46.060
By the way, have we met before?

00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:46.890
No.

00:18:47.310 --> 00:18:48.440
Really?

00:18:48.440 --> 00:18:49.900
That's fine then.

00:18:49.900 --> 00:18:51.650
So where's our girl?

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:54.150
Inside.

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:01.990
Where?

00:19:01.990 --> 00:19:03.780
Inside the bathroom.

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:10.040
<i>So he's going to hand me over to the man who's trying to kill me?</i>

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:13.040
<i>He's going to hand me over and collect his money!</i>

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:15.050
<i>That's what he was planning all along?</i>

00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:20.760
If you want get rid of that girl, you'll have to get rid of me first.

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:30.850
Look pal.

00:19:30.850 --> 00:19:34.610
I'm not sure what's you're up to, but why don't we join forces?

00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:39.820
Paris is an ideal place to spread germs.

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:44.620
We can quickly envelope Paris with the contagion, silencing the city forever!

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:50.620
We'll finally knock those who say France has never lost to us off their high horses!

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:56.090
So, are you going to join me and complete this game?

00:19:56.090 --> 00:19:58.380
Not interested.

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:03.220
I'm only interested in completing my assignment.

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:06.140
To get rid of a certain double-crosser.

00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:08.140
What?

00:20:08.140 --> 00:20:10.390
So that's why you called me here?

00:20:14.060 --> 00:20:16.900
N... Now I remember!

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:19.570
You popped up in the organization's secret documents!

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:19.940
Go...

00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:22.030
Golgo!

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:09.160
M... Mister?

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:11.410
Mister?!

00:21:19.420 --> 00:21:22.670
I have to wait until he gets away from here.

00:21:29.140 --> 00:21:29.550
Sara!

00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:30.930
Papa?

00:21:31.600 --> 00:21:34.180
Sara! You were here?

00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:36.940
Wh... What happened?

00:21:37.270 --> 00:21:38.270
I'm calling the police!

00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:41.020
Sara, are you hurt?!

00:21:41.650 --> 00:21:44.280
Papa, I...

00:21:44.280 --> 00:21:45.780
I'm so sorry.

00:21:45.780 --> 00:21:48.530
I've stopped paying attention to you ever since your Mama passed away.

00:21:50.450 --> 00:21:53.790
But I thank God that you're all right!

00:21:54.200 --> 00:21:55.000
Papa!

00:22:40.670 --> 00:22:45.800
I enjoyed the little things.

00:22:47.840 --> 00:22:53.010
I loved when you gave me a flower every day

00:22:53.760 --> 00:22:59.100
instead of just one big bouquet

00:22:59.810 --> 00:23:03.940
of flowers.

00:23:06.030 --> 00:23:11.570
It was like a romance novel.

00:23:12.200 --> 00:23:16.160
Surely someday... just kidding.

00:23:16.490 --> 00:23:19.540
I had a dream.

00:23:19.920 --> 00:23:25.250
Your face shined eternally.

00:23:26.090 --> 00:23:31.840
Because I think of you all the time.

00:23:32.260 --> 00:23:37.390
I'm sorry, but on a lonely night like this

00:23:38.350 --> 00:23:43.900
I'm remembering you, but

00:23:44.190 --> 00:23:48.490
I won't cry like I did that day.

00:23:50.240 --> 00:23:51.660
I won't.

00:24:02.460 --> 00:24:07.500
Ash is a self-styled artist who creates nothing but junk art.

00:24:07.500 --> 00:24:12.680
Golgo approached him saying he wants to buy everything he made.

00:24:13.510 --> 00:24:16.970
What exactly is Golgo up to this time?

00:24:17.430 --> 00:24:19.930
What is in store for Ash?

00:24:20.810 --> 00:24:25.230
Next time on Golgo 13: The Best Day of Ash's Life.

00:24:21.690 --> 00:24:27.480
The Best Day of Ash's Life

00:24:25.230 --> 00:24:29.030
Don't stand behind him, if you value your life.
